      "index": "a68",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 997084402,
      "version": 318,
      "versionNonce": 550628846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779887192721,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The firmware has the following vulnerabilities:\n- Hardcoded secrets\n- No anti-reverse engineering measures\n- The controller does not prevent reading of the\nflash memory\n- The controller has debugging interfaces\n(JTAG/UART) enabled\n- Embedded within the firmware are files that\nare used; among them, the server's source code\nin C is inadvertently exposed. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "qz98Kb_ZvpqXZtnlkf6mh",
      "originalText": "The firmware has the following vulnerabilities:\n- Hardcoded secrets\n- No anti-reverse engineering measures\n- The controller does not prevent reading of the flash memory\n- The controller has debugging interfaces (JTAG/UART) enabled\n- Embedded within the firmware are files that are used; among them, the server's source code in C is inadvertently exposed. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
